From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Honor immediate native VI display disable without owner retirement
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: native VI display register and real output worker lifecycle.

Implement original STM's VI_DCR=0 ENB request independently of deferred source
VISetBlack, framebuffer/flush ownership, field clocks and PI_VI callbacks.
An attached output requires an explicit operation; unavailable device support
fails before register mutation. A real output failure remains explicit and
retryable without inventing a Present or rolling back the requested register.

Latch the output disable against an already-started Present using a dedicated
gate, keeping normal source prepare/commit and observer mutex scopes brief.
Drain actual queued work and request a real black surface before acknowledging
a presentable display. Only actual successful Present updates its observers.
Unpresentable windows retain their honest last completion. No owners, snapshots,
interrupt handlers or source tasks are retired by this operation.

Original cached VIConfigure ENB=1 re-enables only on its genuine Mode flush;
ordinary retraces, VISetBlack, unflushed requests and idempotent VIInit do not.
Historical output devices may omit the callback until this operation is used.
Default non-native Aurora builds retain explicit unsupported display control.
No ResetTask, OSShutdown or terminal readiness is supplied.

